# MCP Wire Protocol
File: mcp/docs/protocol.oot

JSON-RPC 2.0 over Content-Length or a raw JSON object. Protocol version `2024-11-05`.

## Envelope

Request: `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"<name>","params":{...}}`

Success: `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":<value>}`

Error: `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"error":{"code":-32601,"message":"..."}}`

id may be a string or a number. Duplicate id returns -32603.

## Error codes

| Code | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| -32600 | Invalid request or not initialized |
| -32601 | Method or tool not found |
| -32602 | Invalid params or schema |
| -32603 | Refused: cap, cancel, or replay |
| -32604 | Tier denies method |
| -32605 | URI outside client roots |
| -32606 | Not modified (ETag) |
| -32607 | Rate limit 100 per 1000 seq (every request with an id, including ping) |

## initialize

Params: protocolVersion, clientInfo `{name, version}`, optional tier `minimal|standard|audit`.

clientName at the params root is not read.

On success the server grants FsReadCap (bit 0) and returns protocolVersion `2024-11-05`.

Sampling is not advertised.

## tools/call

params.name is the tool. params.arguments is a JSON object, not a string.

Unknown tool: -32601. Schema miss: -32602. Missing cap: -32603.

## resources

Seven URIs: ooda://orientation, /graph, /header, /boards, /capabilities, /redteam, ooda://em/metrics.

em/metrics requires audit tier. Registry catalog is not served.

## prompts

`prompts/list` returns the `orientation` template. `prompts/get` with `name=orientation` returns messages. Unknown names return -32601.

## roots

`notifications/roots/list_changed` params.uri is appended. `roots/list` returns the declared URIs.

## ETag

`resources/read` with `ifNoneMatch` equal to the 8-char gold-master SHA prefix returns -32606.

## batch

A JSON array is a batch. Notifications in the array are executed. They produce no response item.

## shutdown and exit

`shutdown` returns null and moves the session to Down. Later methods return -32600 except `exit`. `exit` is a notification and closes the session.

## ping

Requires Ready. Returns pong, phase, tier, request_seq, caps_held, bytes_in, bytes_out, protocol.
